{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "With only two completed experiments, the evidence is very sparse. config_016 (multimodal, resnet50, concat) outperforms config_001 (RNA-only) by ~4.2% accuracy, but we cannot yet determine whether this gain comes from the image modality alone or from the synergistic combination of both modalities. config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) is the critical ablation: it isolates the image contribution using the same encoder and profile setting as config_016. If image-only approaches or exceeds the multimodal result, the RNA channel adds little value and future budget should focus on image encoder/architecture choices. If image-only is substantially lower, the fusion is truly synergistic and we should invest in refining fusion strategy and multiprofile aggregation. This single experiment resolves the most fundamental uncertainty in the search space and will most efficiently guide all subsequent decisions under the limited budget."
}

